    "PublishedSheet__MarksNote" : "THE SHEET'S FURNITURE, RESOLVED. The border, the title block and its cells, the wordmark and the QR block, as a display list the reader emits one element at a time. It lays nothing out: the authoring side positions all of this with Na__LeChrome__ (SheetChrome), measuring and fitting every string, and the PUBLISHER runs that same code and writes down what it produced. Parity is therefore guaranteed by construction rather than hoped for - and the reader cannot import SheetChrome anyway, because SheetChrome transitively reaches the snapshot renderer.",
